{"duration_api_ms":30716,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e25384fd-252d-4aef-838b-cacaa052010e","total_cost_usd":0.4919694,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41269,"cache_read_input_tokens":478607,"output_tokens":3304,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1328},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41269,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":593,"cache_read_input_tokens":254060,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11756},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3304,"cacheReadInputTokens":478607,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41269,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4919694,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1328,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json` with one row: **BLANK, `direction-only`**.\n\n**Evidence:** Owens voted Yea on SB 100 (2023 General Session), School Gender Identity Policies. The vote was the Senate concurrence and final passage, which passed 22–6 with 1 absent.\n- About 21% of the senate voted No, so it is not `near-unanimous`.\n- It is a Senate vote, which is the same legislature as his seat, so it counts as `in-term`.\n- I coded both passages (the vote page and the bill text) as one record group, with `record_kind` \"vote\".\n- `actor_quote`: \"Millner, A. Owens, D.R. Sandall, S.\"\n- `tally_quote`: \"Yeas 22 Nays 6 Abs 1\"\n- `provision_quote`: section (3)(a)–(b) of the bill text, copied verbatim with the PDF line numbers left in.\n\n**Why blank:** The bill's operative section stops schools from shielding a student's education record from parents. It also bars changes to the record's gender-identity entry \"without written parental consent.\" That puts Owens against rungs 1 and 2, but it does not choose among rungs 3, 4 and 5:\n- The bill is about the education record. It does not require schools to tell parents on their own (rung 4).\n- It does not govern which name or pronouns staff use (rung 5's object).\n- It says nothing that rules either of those rungs out, and ruling out the other rungs would not be evidence for rung 3 anyway (V4.2).\n\n**`needs_source`:** Owens's own words on telling parents or asking their consent, or any bill he acted on that requires schools to notify parents, or parental permission before staff use a different name or pronouns.\n\nThere are no candidate quotes, because both sources are records.","ttft_ms":14475,"type":"result","duration_ms":32483,"uuid":"b7ca5165-2392-4b7e-8da4-64ce2261b561","ttft_stream_ms":1404,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":1404,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
